    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "The drawbacks next: spice-like portions cap the real payoff. The numbers are huge, but the real serving is tiny. Strong flavour can take over a dish. That anise-like taste is useful, but it is not exactly neutral. Whole seeds can be awkward to eat. Texture and chewing matter, especially when they are sprinkled in rather than ground.",
